---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const cndBook = 'https://michael-borck.github.io/conversation-not-delegation';
const partnerBook = 'https://michael-borck.github.io/partner-dont-police';
const substantiateBook = 'https://michael-borck.github.io/substantiate-dont-assume';
const humanEdge = 'https://thehumanedge.borck.dev';
const books = 'https://books.borck.education';
const consulting = 'https://borck.consulting/services';
---
<Base>

<header class="topbar">
  <a class="wordmark" href="/">Conversation, <span>Not Delegation</span></a>
  <nav class="nav">
    <a href={humanEdge}>The Human Edge</a>
    <a href={books}>Books</a>
    <a href={consulting}>Consulting</a>
  </nav>
</header>

<main>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">A framework · Michael Borck</p>
      <h1>Conversation,<br /><span>not Delegation.</span></h1>
      <p class="subtitle">How to think with AI, not just use it.</p>
      <p class="lead">Delegation outsources judgment. Conversation preserves it.</p>
      <p class="body">
        A problem arrives. The work is handed to a model. A polished result comes back.
        The work appears to be done. The cost is not in the output. It is in what stops
        happening in the head of the person who used to do the work.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href={cndBook}>Read the book</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={humanEdge}>The workplace book</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-cover">
      <img
        src="/covers/conversation-not-delegation.png"
        alt="Conversation, Not Delegation: How to Think With AI, Not Just Use It by Michael Borck"
        width="600"
        height="900"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pullquote">
    <p>The work that used to happen quietly stays where it should: in the head of the practitioner.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="section-kicker">The problem</p>
    <h2>Delegation looks efficient. It is not free.</h2>
    <div class="split">
      <p>
        A fluent answer is not the same as a considered one. The output is often
        serviceable. The judgment behind it is what disappears when the work is handed
        over without a conversation.
      </p>
      <p>
        The small, quiet activity between problem and answer is the substance of
        professional practice. Conversation keeps it in the practitioner. Delegation
        moves it into the model and hopes nobody notices.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="section-kicker">The conversation loop</p>
    <h2>Four moves, one loop.</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="card-num">01</p>
        <h3>Brainstorm</h3>
        <p>Define the question. Arrive with a problem worth thinking about, not a task to outsource.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="card-num">02</p>
        <h3>Ideate</h3>
        <p>Explore possibilities. Use the model's breadth, but do not stop at the first interesting output.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="card-num">03</p>
        <h3>Iterate</h3>
        <p>Push back and refine. Correct course. Disagree on substance. Stay here longer than feels necessary.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="card-num">04</p>
        <h3>Amplify</h3>
        <p>Make it yours. Edit, restructure, combine, and cut until you would put your name on it.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="section-kicker">The books</p>
    <h2>The framework, and the companions.</h2>
    <div class="book-grid">
      <a class="book-card" href={cndBook}>
        <img src="/covers/conversation-not-delegation.png" alt="Conversation, Not Delegation book cover" loading="lazy" />
        <span class="book-title">Conversation, Not Delegation</span>
        <span class="book-sub">How to Think With AI, Not Just Use It</span>
      </a>
      <a class="book-card" href={partnerBook}>
        <img src="/covers/partner-dont-police.png" alt="Partner, Don't Police book cover" loading="lazy" />
        <span class="book-title">Partner, Don't Police</span>
        <span class="book-sub">AI in the Business Classroom</span>
      </a>
      <a class="book-card" href={substantiateBook}>
        <img src="/covers/substantiate-dont-assume.png" alt="Substantiate, Don't Assume book cover" loading="lazy" />
        <span class="book-title">Substantiate, Don't Assume</span>
        <span class="book-sub">Why the Auditor's Opinion Matters More Than Ever in the Age of AI</span>
      </a>
      <a class="book-card" href={humanEdge}>
        <img src="/covers/the-human-edge.png" alt="The Human Edge book cover" loading="lazy" />
        <span class="book-title">The Human Edge</span>
        <span class="book-sub">Using AI with Judgement</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="book-more">
      All books are free to download at <a href={books}>books.borck.education</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section bridge">
    <div>
      <p class="section-kicker">The workplace book</p>
      <h2>The Human Edge.</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        When everyone has the same AI tools, generic competence is the baseline. The
        edge is judgement. The Human Edge is the companion for professionals who have
        to sign their name to the output.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn" href={humanEdge}>Read The Human Edge</a>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="section-kicker">In practice</p>
    <h2>Applying this in a regulated firm is different work.</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">
      Reading the framework is one thing. Changing how a firm briefs, checks, and signs
      off AI-assisted work is another. That is what borck.consulting is for.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href={consulting}>See the consulting practice →</a>
  </section>

</main>

<footer class="footer">
  <p>Michael Borck · <a href="mailto:michael@borck.dev">michael@borck.dev</a></p>
  <p class="footer-links">
    <a href={humanEdge}>The Human Edge</a>
    <a href={books}>Books</a>
    <a href={consulting}>Consulting</a>
    <a href="https://borck.dev">borck.dev</a>
  </p>
</footer>

</Base>
